:: place.civil-office
@hub civil_office

Counters, forms, and noticeboards fill {{place.name}}.

@choicegroup notice-quest ""
@choice notice-question "Ask about the notice" -> story.rent.intro.1
    @time 10m
    @when flags.home_notice_read and not flags.home_notice_resolved
    @effect flag home_notice_resolved true
    @effect reminder clear home_rent_notice_1
@endchoice
@endchoicegroup


:: story.rent.intro.1 -> @exit
  "Um, hello?" You hold the notice up to the receptionist. "I found this on my door. What is it about?"

  The receptionist looks at the notice, then back at you. "Oh, yes. That is a notice about your rent. It seems that you have not paid your rent for the last two months." @change stat stress 25

  @next

  "What? That can't be right! I just moved here!" you say. @change stat mind -10

  "Well, the notice is clear. You have not paid your rent for the last two months. You need to pay it as soon as possible, or you will be evicted," the receptionist says.
  "Frankly, I don't know what to tell you. You should probably check your records and make sure that you have paid your rent. If you have, then you should contact the landlord and let them know.", she shurgs, unsympathetic.

  She turns away and starts talking to another person. You are left standing there, feeling confused and frustrated.

  @next

  Inspecting the notice, you see a phone number at the bottom. Is that your landlord? 

  You add it to your contacts. You can message Kim through the Chats app on your phone.
  @effect contact add "kim"
  @effect chat start kim.rent
  
  @next -> @exit
